From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erich Seifert <dev@erichseifert.de>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:08:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Record proxy renders in the PostProject sidecar

When a proxy is rendered for a clip the sidecar knows, request a proxy
job and claim it with Kdenlive as the worker, renewing the claim while
ffmpeg or melt runs. A finished render records the proxy as a
representation of the clip, together with an activity naming the tool
and its arguments, and completes the job in the same transaction. A
failed render fails the job with the end of its log, and an abandoned
one cancels it.

Proxies made before their clip was recorded, such as those of a
project saved for the first time, are recorded on save when their name
carries the clip's present Kdenlive hash.

